<article class="env-definition" id="06KD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06KD">Definition <span data-tag="06KD">90.22.1</span>.</a> A groupoid in functors on $\mathcal{C}_\Lambda $ is <em>prorepresentable</em> if it is isomorphic to $(\underline{R_0}, \underline{R_1}, s, t, c)|_{\mathcal{C}_\Lambda }$ for some representable groupoid in functors $(\underline{R_0}, \underline{R_1}, s, t, c)$ on the category $\widehat{\mathcal{C}}_\Lambda $. </p>
